3. As you inspirez, Lentement, lower the platform until your upper and lower legs make a angle de 90 degrés.
4. Pushing mainly with the heels of vos pieds and using the quadriceps go back to the position de départ as you expirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. and ensure to lock the safety pins properly once you are done. You do not want that platform falling on you fully loaded.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Narrow_Stance_Leg_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Narrow Stance Squats', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. cet exercice is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your épaules (slightly below the neck) across it.
2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse.
3. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a less-than-épaule-width narrow stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Feet should be around 3-6 inches apart. Keep votre tête up en permanence (looking down will get you off balance) and maintain a straight back. C''est votre position de départ. (Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance described above which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances discussed in the foot stances section).
4. Begin to Lentement, lower the bar by bending the genous as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the mollets becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallèle au sol). Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genous should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendiculaire à the front. If your genous are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genou and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.
5. Begin to raise the bar as you expirez by pushing le sol with the heel of your foot mainly as you straighten the legs again and go back to the position de départ.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Narrow_Stance_Squats/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Natural Glute Ham Raise', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Poids de corps', '1. Using the leg pad of a lat pulldown machine or a preacher banc, position yourself so that your chevilles are under the pads, genous on the seat, and you are facing away from the machine. You should be upright and maintaining good posture.
2. C''est votre position de départ. Lower yourself under control until your genous are almost completely straight.
3. Remaining in control, raise yourself back up to the position de départ.
4. If you are unable to complete a rep, use a band, a partner, or push off of a box to aid in completing a repetition.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Natural_Glute_Ham_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Neck-SMR', 'Cou', 'Autre', '1. Using a muscle roller or a rolling pin, place the roller behind votre tête and against your neck. Make sure that you do not place the roller directly against the spine, but turned slightly so that the roller is pressed against the muscles to either side of the spine. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Starting at the top of your neck, Lentement, roll down the muscles of your neck, pausing at points of tension for 10-30 seconds.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Neck-SMR/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Neck Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Barre', '1. Allongez-vous au sol on a flat banc. Using a medium-width grip (a grip that creates a angle de 90 degrés in the middle of le mouvement between the forearms and the upper arms), lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over your neck with vos bras locked. C''est votre position de départ.
2. As you Inspirez, come down Lentement, until you feel the bar on your neck.
3. Après une pause, bring the bar back to the position de départ as you Expirez and push the bar using your poitrine muscles. Lock vos bras and squeeze your poitrine in the contracted position, Maintenez la position 1 seconde and then start coming down Lentement, again. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up).
4. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.
5. When you are done, place the bar back in the rack.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Neck_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Oblique Crunches', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Allongez-vous au sol with your lower back pressed to the ground. For cet exercice, you will need to put one hand beside votre tête and the other to the side against le sol.
2. Make sure vos pieds are elevated and resting on a flat surface.
3. Now lift the épaule in which your hand is touching votre tête.
4. Simply elevate your épaule and body upward until you touch your genou. For example, if you have your right hand besides votre tête, then you want to elevate votre corps upwards until your right coude touches your left genou. The same variation can be applied doing the inverse and using your left coude to touch your right genou.
5. After your genou touches your coude, lower votre corps until you have reached the position de départ.
6. Remember to Inspirez during the eccentric (lowering) part of the exercise and to Expirez during the concentric (upward) part of the exercise.
7. Continue alternating in this manner until all of the recommended repetitions for each side have been completed.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Oblique_Crunches/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Oblique Crunches - On The Floor', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Start out by lying on your right side with vos jambes lying on top of each other. Make sure your genous are bent a little bit.
2. Place your left hand behind votre tête.
3. Once you are in this set position, begin by moving your left coude up as you would perform a normal crunch except this time the main emphasis is on your obliques.
4. Crunch as high as you can, hold the contraction for a second and then Lentement, drop back down into the position de départ.
5. Remember to Inspirez during the eccentric (lowering) part of the exercise and to Expirez during the concentric (elevation) part of the exercise.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Oblique_Crunches_-_On_The_Floor/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Olympic Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a barre supported on top of the traps. The poitrine should be up, and the head facing forward. Adopt a hanche width stance with the feet turned out as needed.
2. Descend by flexing the genous, refraining from moving the hanches back as much as possible. This requires that the genous travel forward; ensure that they stay aligned with the feet. The goal is to keep the torse as upright as possible. Continue all the way down, keeping the poids on the front of the heel.
3. At the moment the upper legs contact the lower, reverse the motion, driving the poids upward.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Olympic_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('On-Your-Back Quad Stretch', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Allongez-vous sur un banc plat or step, and hang one leg and arm over the side.
2. Bend the genou and hold the top of the foot. As you do this, be careful not to arch your lower back.
3. Pull the belly button to the spine to stay in neutral. Press your foot down and into your hand. To add the hanche stretch, lift the hanche of the leg you''re holding up toward the ceiling.
4. Switch sides.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/On-Your-Back_Quad_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('On Your Side Quad Stretch', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Start off by lying on your right side, with your right genou bent at a angle de 90 degrés resting on le sol in front of you (this stabilizes the torse).
2. Bend your left genou behind you and hold your left foot with your left hand. To stretch your hanche flexor, press your left hanche forward as you push your left foot back into your hand. Switch sides.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/On_Your_Side_Quad_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Dumbbell Row', 'Milieu du dos', 'Haltères', '1. Choose a flat banc and place a haltère on each side of it.
2. Place the right leg on top of the end of the banc, bend your torse forward from the waist until your upper body is parallèle au sol, and place your right hand on the other end of the banc for support.
3. Use the left hand to pick up the haltère on le sol and hold the poids while keeping your lower back straight. The palm of the hand should be facing your torse. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Pull the resistance straight up to the side of your poitrine, keeping your upper arm close to your side and keeping the torse stationary. Expirez as you perform this step. Conseil : Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. Also, make sure that the force is performed with the back muscles and not the arms. Finally, the upper torse should remain stationary and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work except for holding the haltère; therefore do not try to pull the haltère up using the forearms.
5. Lower the resistance straight down to the position de départ. Inspirez as you perform this step.
6. Répétez le mouvement for the specified amount of repetitions.
7. Switch sides and Répétez again with the other arm.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Dumbbell_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Flat Bench Dumbbell Flye', 'Pectoraux', 'Haltères', '1. Allongez-vous sur un banc plat with a haltère in one hand resting on top of your cuisse. The palm of your hand with the haltère in it should be at a neutral grip.
2. By using your cuisses to help you get the haltère up, clean the haltère so that you can hold it in front of you with your lifting arm being fully extended. Remember to maintain a neutral grip with cet exercice. Your non lifting hand should be to the side holding the flat banc for better support. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Your arm with the poids should have a slight bend on your coude in order to prevent stress at the biceps tendon. Begin by lowering your arm with the poids in it out in a wide arc until you feel a stretch on your poitrine. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : Keep in mind that throughout le mouvement, your lifting arm should remain stationary; le mouvement should only occur at the épaule joint.
4. Return your lifting arm back to the position de départ as you squeeze your poitrine muscles and Expirez. Conseil : Make sure to use the same arc of motion used to lower the poids.
5. Maintenez la position 1 seconde at the contracted position and Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.
6. Switch arms and Répétez the exercise.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Flat_Bench_Dumbbell_Flye/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm High-Pulley Cable Side Bends', 'Abdominaux', 'Poulie', '1. Connect a standard handle to a tower. Move cable to highest pulley position.
2. Tenez-vous debout avec side to cable. With one hand, reach up and grab handle with prise en supination.
3. Pull down cable until coude touches your side and the handle is by your épaule.
4. Position feet hanche-width apart. Place free hand on hanche to help gauge pivot point.
5. Keep arm in static position. Contract oblique to bring the poids down in a side crunch.
6. Once you reach maximum contraction, Lentement, release the poids to the position de départ. The poids stack should never be unloaded in a resting position. The aim is constant tension during the set.
7. Répétez to failure.
8. Then, reposition and Répétez the same series of movements on the opposite side.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_High-Pulley_Cable_Side_Bends/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Incline Lateral Raise', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Lie down sideways on an incline banc press with a haltère in the hand. Make sure the épaule is pressing against the incline banc and the arm is lying across votre corps with the palm around your navel.
2. Hold a haltère in your uppermost arm while keeping it extended in front of you parallèle au sol. C''est votre position de départ.
3. While keeping the haltère parallèle au sol en permanence, perform a lateral raise. Your arm should travel straight up until it is pointing at the ceiling. Conseil : Expirez as you perform this movement. Hold the haltère in the position and feel the contraction in the épaules for a second.
4. While inhaling lower the poids across votre corps back into the position de départ.
5. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.
6. Switch arms and Répétez le mouvement.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Incline_Lateral_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Kettlebell Clean', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Kettlebell', '1. Place a kettlebell between vos pieds. As you bend down to grab the kettlebell, push your butt back and keep your eyes looking forward.
2. Clean the kettlebell to your épaules by extending through the legs and hanches as you raise the kettlebell towards your épaule. The poignet should rotate as you do so.
3. Return the poids to the position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Bas du dos, Épaules, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Clean/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Kettlebell Clean and Jerk', 'Épaules', 'Kettlebell', '1. Hold a kettlebell by the handle.
2. Clean the kettlebell to your épaule by extending through the legs and hanches as you pull the kettlebell towards your épaule. Rotate your poignet as you do so, so that the palm faces forward.
3. Dip votre corps by bending the genous, keeping your torse upright.
4. Immediately reverse direction, driving through the heels, in essence jumping to create momentum. As you do so, press the kettlebell overhead to lockout by extending the arms, using votre corps''s momentum to move the poids.
5. Receive the poids overhead by returning to a squat position underneath the poids.
6. Keeping the poids overhead, return to a standing position. Lower the poids to le sol to perform the next repetition.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Clean_and_Jerk/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Kettlebell Floor Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Kettlebell', '1. Allongez-vous au sol holding a kettlebell with one hand, with your upper arm supported by le sol. The palm should be facing in.
2. Press the kettlebell straight up toward the ceiling, rotating your poignet.
3. Lower the kettlebell back to the position de départ and Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Floor_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Kettlebell Jerk', 'Épaules', 'Kettlebell', '1. Hold a kettlebell by the handle. Clean the kettlebell to your épaule by extending through the legs and hanches as you pull the kettlebell towards your épaule. Rotate your poignet as you do so, so that the palm faces forward. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Dip votre corps by bending the genous, keeping your torse upright.
3. Immediately reverse direction, driving through the heels, in essence jumping to create momentum. As you do so, press the kettlebell overhead to lockout by extending the arms, using votre corps''s momentum to move the poids. Receive the poids overhead by returning to a squat position underneath the poids. Keeping the poids overhead, return to a standing position.
4. Lower the poids to perform the next repetition.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Quadriceps, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Jerk/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Kettlebell Military Press To The Side', 'Épaules', 'Kettlebell', '1. Clean a kettlebell to your épaule. Clean the kettlebell to your épaule by extending through the legs and hanches as you pull the kettlebell towards your épaule. Rotate your poignet as you do so, so that the palm faces inward. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Look at the kettlebell and press it up and out until it is locked out overhead.
3. Lower the kettlebell back to your épaule under control and Répétez. Make sure to contract your lat, butt, and stomach forcefully for added stability and strength.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Military_Press_To_The_Side/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Kettlebell Para Press', 'Épaules', 'Kettlebell', '1. Clean a kettlebell to your épaule. Clean the kettlebell to your épaule by extending through the legs and hanches as you pull the kettlebell towards your épaule. Rotate your poignet as you do so, so that the palm faces forward. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Hold the kettlebell with the coude out to the side, and press it up and out until it is locked out overhead.
3. Lower the kettlebell back to your épaule under control and Répétez. Make sure to contract your lat, butt, and stomach forcefully for added stability and strength.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Para_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Kettlebell Push Press', 'Épaules', 'Kettlebell', '1. Hold a kettlebell by the handle. Clean the kettlebell to your épaule by extending through the legs and hanches as you pull the kettlebell towards your épaule. Rotate your poignet as you do so, so that the palm faces forward. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Dip votre corps by bending the genous, keeping your torse upright.
3. Immediately reverse direction, driving through the heels, in essence jumping to create momentum. As you do so, press the kettlebell overhead to lockout by extending the arms, using votre corps''s momentum to move the poids. Lower the poids to perform the next repetition.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Quadriceps, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Push_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Kettlebell Row', 'Milieu du dos', 'Kettlebell', '1. Place a kettlebell in front of vos pieds. Bend your genous slightly and then push your butt out as much as possible as you bend over to get in the position de départ. Grab the kettlebell and pull it to your stomach, retracting your omoplates and flexing the coude. Keep votre dos straight. Lower and Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Kettlebell Snatch', 'Épaules', 'Kettlebell', '1. Place a kettlebell between vos pieds. Bend your genous and push your butt back to get in the proper position de départ.
2. Look straight ahead and swing the kettlebell back between vos jambes.
3. Immediately reverse the direction and drive through with your hanches and genous, accelerating the kettlebell upward. As the kettlebell rises to your épaule rotate your hand and punch straight up, using momentum to receive the poids locked out overhead.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Trapèzes, Triceps. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Snatch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Kettlebell Split Jerk', 'Épaules', 'Kettlebell', '1. Hold a kettlebell by the handle. Clean the kettlebell to your épaule by extending through the legs and hanches as you pull the kettlebell towards your épaule. Rotate your poignet as you do so, so that the palm faces forward. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Dip votre corps by bending the genous, keeping your torse upright.
3. Immediately reverse direction, driving through the heels, in essence jumping to create momentum. As you do so, press the kettlebell overhead to lockout by extending the arms, using votre corps''s momentum to move the poids.
4. Receive the poids overhead by returning to a squat position underneath the poids, positioning one leg in front of you and one leg behind you.
5. Keeping the poids overhead, return to a standing position and bring vos pieds together. Lower the poids to perform the next repetition.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Quadriceps, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Split_Jerk/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Kettlebell Split Snatch', 'Épaules', 'Kettlebell', '1. Hold a kettlebell in one hand by the handle.
2. Squat towards le sol, and then reverse the motion, extending the hanches, genous, and finally the chevilles, to raise the kettlebell overhead.
3. After fully extending the body, descend into a lunge position to receive the poids overhead, one leg forward and one leg back. Ensure you drive through with your hanches and lock the ketttlebells overhead in one uninterrupted motion.
4. Return to a standing position, holding the poids overhead, and bring the feet together. Lower the poids to Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Ischio-jambiers, Quadriceps. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Split_Snatch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Kettlebell Swings', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Kettlebell', '', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Swings/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Long Bar Row', 'Milieu du dos', 'Barre', '1. Position a bar into a landmine or in a corner to keep it from moving. Load an appropriate poids onto your end.
2. Stand next to the bar, and take a grip with one hand close to the collar. Using your hanches and legs, rise to a standing position.
3. Assume a bent-genou stance with your hanches back and your poitrine up. Your arm should be extended. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Pull the poids to your side by retracting the épaule and flexing the coude. Do not jerk the poids or cheat during le mouvement.
5. Après une pause, Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Long_Bar_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Medicine Ball Slam', 'Abdominaux', 'Medecine ball', '1. Start in a standing position with a staggered, athletic stance. Hold a medicine ball in one hand, on the same side as votre dos leg. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin by winding the arm, raising the medicine ball above votre tête. As you do so, extend through the hanches, genous, and chevilles to load up for the slam.
3. At peak extension, flex the épaules, spine, and hanches to throw the ball hard into the ground directly in front of you.
4. Catch the ball on the bounce and continue for the desired number of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Dos, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Medicine_Ball_Slam/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Open Palm Kettlebell Clean', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Kettlebell', '1. Place one kettlebell between vos pieds.
2. Grab the handle with one hand and raise the kettlebell rapidly, let it flip so that the ball of the kettlebell lands in the palm of your hand.
3. Throw the kettlebell out in front of you and catch the handle with one hand.
4. Take the kettlebell to le sol and Répétez. Make sure to work both arms.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Open_Palm_Kettlebell_Clean/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Overhead Kettlebell Squats', 'Quadriceps', 'Kettlebell', '1. Clean and press a kettlebell with one arm. Clean the kettlebell to your épaule by extending through the legs and hanches as you pull the kettlebell towards your épaule. Rotate your poignet as you do so. Press the poids overhead by extending through the coude.C''est votre position de départ.
2. Looking straight ahead and keeping a kettlebell locked out above you, flex the genous and hanches and lower your torse between vos jambes, keeping votre tête and poitrine up.
3. Pause at the bottom position for a second before rising back to the top, driving through the heels of vos pieds.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Épaules. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Overhead_Kettlebell_Squats/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Side Deadlift', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Stand to the side of a barre next to its center. Bend your genous and lower votre corps until you are able to reach the barre.
2. Grasp the bar as if you were grabbing a briefcase (paumes vers you since the bar is sideways). You may need a poignet wrap if you are using a significant amount of poids. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Use vos jambes to help lift the barre up while exhaling. vos bras should extend fully as bring the barre up until you are in a standing position.
4. Lentement, bring the barre back down while inhaling. Conseil : Make sure to bend your genous while lowering the poids to avoid any injury from occurring.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.
6. Switch arms and Répétez le mouvement.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Trapèzes. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Side_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Arm Side Laterals', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Pick a haltère and place it in one of vos mains. Your non lifting hand should be used to grab something steady such as an incline banc press. Lean towards your lifting arm and away from the hand that is gripping the incline banc as this will allow you to keep your balance.
2. Tenez-vous debout avec a straight torse and have the haltère by your side at arm''s length with the palm of the hand facing you. C''est votre position de départ.
3. While maintaining the torse stationary (no swinging), lift the haltère to your side with a slight bend on the coude and your hand slightly tilted forward as if pouring water in a glass. Continue to go up until you arm is parallèle au sol. Expirez as you execute this movement and pause for a second at the top.
4. Lower the haltère back down Lentement, to the position de départ as you inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.
6. Switch arms and Répétez the exercise.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Arm_Side_Laterals/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One-Legged Cable Kickback', 'Fessiers', 'Poulie', '1. Hook a leather cheville cuff to a low cable pulley and then attach the cuff to your cheville.
2. Face the poids stack from a distance of about two feet, grasping the steel frame for support.
3. While keeping your genous and hanches bent slightly and your abdominaux tight, contract your fessiers to Lentement, "kick" the working leg back in a semicircular arc as high as it will comfortably go as you Expirez. Conseil : At full extension, squeeze your fessiers for a second in order to achieve a peak contraction.
4. Now Lentement, bring your working leg forward, resisting the pull of the cable until you reach the position de départ.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.
6. Switch legs and Répétez le mouvement for the other side.', 'Muscles secondaires : Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One-Legged_Cable_Kickback/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One Arm Against Wall', 'Dos', 'Autre', '1. From a standing position, place a bent arm against a wall or doorway.
2. Lentement, lean toward your arm until you feel a stretch in your lats.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One_Arm_Against_Wall/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One Arm Chin-Up', 'Milieu du dos', 'Autre', '1. For cet exercice, start out by placing a towel around a chin up bar.
2. Grab the chin-up bar with your paumes vers you. One hand will be grabbing the chin-up bar and the other will be grabbing the towel.
3. Bring your torse back around 30 degrees or so while creating a curvature on your lower back and sticking your poitrine out. C''est votre position de départ.v
4. Pull your torse up until the bar touches your upper poitrine by drawing the épaules and the upper arms down and back. Expirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torse should remain stationary as it moves through space and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work other than hold the bar.
5. After a second on the contracted position, start to inspirez and Lentement, lower your torse back to the position de départ when vos bras are fully extended and the lats are fully stretched.
6. Répétez this motion for the prescribed amount of repetitions.
7. Switch arms and Répétez le mouvement.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Avant-bras, Dos. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One_Arm_Chin-Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One Arm Dumbbell Bench Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Haltères', '1. Allongez-vous sur un banc plat with a haltère in one hand on top of your cuisse.
2. By using your cuisse to help you get the haltère up, clean the haltère up so that you can hold it in front of you at épaule width. Use the hand you are not lifting with to help position the haltère over you properly.
3. Once at épaule width, rotate your poignet forward so that the palm of your hand is facing away from you. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Bring down the poids Lentement, to your side as you Inspirez. Keep full control of the haltère en permanence. Conseil : Use the hand that you are not lifting with to help keep the haltère balance as you may struggle a bit at first. Only use your non-lifting hand if it is needed. Otherwise, keep it resting to the side.
5. As you Expirez, push the haltères up using your pectoral muscles. Lock vos bras in the contracted position, squeeze your poitrine, Maintenez la position 1 seconde and then start coming down slowly. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.
6. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions of your training program.
7. Switch arms and Répétez le mouvement.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One_Arm_Dumbbell_Bench_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One Arm Dumbbell Preacher Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Grab a haltère with the right arm and place the upper arm on top of the preacher banc or the incline banc. The haltère should be held at épaule length. C''est votre position de départ.
2. As you Inspirez, Lentement, lower the haltère until your upper arm is extended and the biceps is fully stretched.
3. As you expirez, use the biceps to curl the poids up until your biceps is entièrement contracté and the haltère is at épaule height. Again, remember that to ensure full contraction you need to bring that small finger higher than the thumb.
4. Squeeze the biceps hard for a second at the contracted position and Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.
5. Switch arms and Répétez le mouvement.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One_Arm_Dumbbell_Preacher_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One Arm Floor Press', 'Triceps', 'Barre', '1. Lie down on a flat surface with votre dos pressing against le sol or an exercise mat. Make sure your genous are bent.
2. Have a partner hand you the bar on one hand. When starting, your arm should be just about fully extended, similar to the position de départ of a barre banc press. However, this time your grip will be neutral (paumes vers your torse).
3. Make sure the hand you are not using to lift the poids is placed by your side.
4. Begin the exercise by lowering the barre until your coude touches the ground. Make sure to Inspirez as this is the eccentric (lowering part of the exercise).
5. Then start lifting the barre back up to the original position de départ. Remember to Expirez during the concentric (lifting part of the exercise).
6. Répétez until you have performed your recommended repetitions.
7. Switch arms and Répétez le mouvement.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One_Arm_Floor_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One Arm Lat Pulldown', 'Dos', 'Poulie', '1. Select an appropriate poids and adjust the genou pad to help keep you down. Grasp the handle with a pronated grip. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Pull the handle down, squeezing your coude to your side as you flex the coude.
3. Pause at the bottom of the motion, and then Lentement, return the handle to the position de départ.
4. For multiple repetitions, avoid completely returning the poids to keep tension on the muscles being worked.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One_Arm_Lat_Pulldown/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One Arm Pronated Dumbbell Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. Lie flat on a banc while holding a haltère bras tendus. Your arm should be perpendiculaire à votre corps. The palm of your hand should be facing towards vos pieds as a pronated grip is required to perform cet exercice.
2. Place your non lifting hand on your biceps for support.
3. Lentement, begin to lower the haltère down as you Inspirez.
4. Then, begin lifting the haltère upward as you contract the triceps. Remember to Expirez during the concentric (lifting part of the exercise).
5. Répétez until you have performed your set repetitions.
6. Switch arms and Répétez le mouvement.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One_Arm_Pronated_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One Arm Supinated Dumbbell Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. Lie flat on a banc while holding a haltère bras tendus. Your arm should be perpendiculaire à votre corps. The palm of your hand should be facing towards your face as a supinated grip is required to perform cet exercice.
2. Place your non lifting hand on your biceps for support.
3. Lentement, begin to lower the haltère down as you Inspirez.
4. Then, begin lifting the haltère upward as you contract the triceps. Remember to Expirez during the concentric (lifting part of the exercise).
5. Répétez until you have performed your set repetitions.
6. Switch arms and Répétez le mouvement.
7. Switch arms again and Répétez le mouvement.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One_Arm_Supinated_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One Half Locust', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Lie facedown on le sol.
2. Put your left hand under your left hipbone to pad your hanche and pubic bone.
3. Bend your right genou so you can hold the foot in your right hand.
4. Lift the foot in the air and simultaneously lift your épaules off le sol. This also stretches the right hanche flexor and the poitrine and épaules. Switch sides. If it doesn''t bother votre dos, you can try it with both arms and legs at the same time.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Biceps, Pectoraux. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One_Half_Locust/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One Handed Hang', 'Dos', 'Autre', '1. Grab onto a chinup bar with one hand, using a pronated grip. Keep vos pieds on le sol or a step. Allow the majority of your poids to hang from that hand, while keeping vos pieds on the ground. Maintenez 10-20 secondes and switch sides.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One_Handed_Hang/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One Knee To Chest', 'Fessiers', 'Autre', '1. Start off by lying on le sol.
2. Extend one leg straight and pull the other genou to your poitrine. Hold under the genou joint to protect the kneecap.
3. Gently tug that genou toward your nose.
4. Switch sides. This stretches the buttocks and lower back of the bent leg and the hanche flexor of the straight leg.', 'Muscles secondaires : Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One_Knee_To_Chest/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('One Leg Barbell Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Start by standing about 2 to 3 feet in front of a flat banc with votre dos facing the banc. Have a barre in front of you on le sol. Conseil : vos pieds should be épaule width apart from each other.
2. Bend the genous and use a pronated grip with vos mains being wider than épaule width apart from each other to lift the barre up until you can rest it on your poitrine.
3. Then lift the barre over votre tête and rest it on the base of your neck. Move one foot back so that your toe is resting on the flat banc. Your other foot should be stationary in front of you. Keep votre tête up en permanence as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. Conseil : Make sure votre dos is straight and poitrine is out while performing cet exercice.
4. As you inspirez, Lentement, lower your leg until your cuisse is parallèle au sol. At this point, your genou should be over your toes. Your poitrine should be directly above the middle of your cuisse.
5. Leading with the poitrine and hanches and contracting the quadriceps, elevate your leg back to the position de départ as you expirez.
